# Eval-audit break surfaces (2026-10-06).
#
# Each case below pins a finding from the evaluation audit to a concrete input,
# so a future engine or harness change that moves one of these verdicts shows
# up as a named baseline regression instead of a silent drift. All forked from
# inputs the audit measured by hand against analyzeContent; the notes record
# the score at commit time and which audit finding the case covers.
#
# au-sms-0017: bare-host sentence guard. "freemoney.tk" loses its URL card to
#   the prose-continuation rule and scores 22 (suspicious) on message signals
#   alone — two points above the safe line. Unit cover in
#   __tests__/bareHostname.test.ts; this is the eval-layer ratchet.
# au-sms-0018 / au-sms-0019: forwarded-prefix is never applied by the
#   metamorphic suite to parcel-delivery / toll / government cases, by category
#   exclusion. These are the composed inputs the harness skips, committed
#   directly: 100 -> 90 and 65 -> 45 respectively at commit time.
# au-sms-0020: card truncation. analyzeContent scores at most 3 URLs per input,
#   so the 4th host is examined by neither the engine nor the eval.
# au-sms-0021: shortener without expansion. The eval stubs the fetcher, so this
#   pins the unexpanded verdict (85 at commit time); prod with a transport
#   takes max(base, destination) and may read higher.
# au-sms-0022: bare host carrying a query string. url-tracking-params only
#   applies to schemed URLs, so this shape has no transform coverage.
# au-sms-0023: callback number in a PII shape the corpus privacy gate does not
#   recognise (parenthesised AU mobile). Declared in "identifiers" anyway, so
#   the case keeps loading if the gate is ever widened to see it. Number is
#   ACMA drama range (0491 570 156-216), never a real subscriber.
# de-sms-0001 / sg-sms-0001: minimal-pack brand impersonation with no
#   open-suffix probe covering the region (probes exist for GB/AU/CA/NZ only).
#   Both abstain under minimal coverage (25 / 45 at commit time) — expected
#   until the packs go full, same standing as ca-sms-0001.
{"id": "au-sms-0017", "type": "sms", "region": "AU", "content": "claim now at freemoney.tk urgently", "label": "scam", "source": "handwritten", "addedAt": "2026-10-06", "notes": "Audit 2026-10-06: bare-host sentence guard suppresses the URL card; scores suspicious (22) on message signals alone. Verdict-only metamorphic relations cannot see further erosion toward the 20-point line."}
{"id": "au-sms-0018", "type": "sms", "region": "AU", "content": "---------- Forwarded message ----------\nFrom: Unknown <unknown@example.invalid>\nDate: 2 Sep 2026\nSubject: Fwd: hi\n\nAusPost: your parcel is held at customs. Pay the outstanding import duty to release your parcel: http://auspost-clearance.cyou/pay", "label": "scam", "category": "parcel-delivery", "source": "handwritten", "addedAt": "2026-10-06", "identifiers": ["unknown@example.invalid"], "notes": "Audit 2026-10-06: the composed input forwarded-prefix would build on a parcel case but never checks (category exclusion). Scores likely_scam (90) vs 100 unforwaded."}
